{
  "dom_id": "question-133289",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "The eagle is descending for all $t$ in the interval\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\,t\\in ($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$).$",
  "worked_solution": "If the eagle is descending, then its vertical velocity is negative.\n\nWe know that the eagle's vertical velocity is given by ${y}^{′}(t)={t}^{2}-2.$\n\nTo calculate the time interval in which the eagle's vertical velocity is decreasing, we solve the inequality ${y}^{′}(t)<0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & <0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-2 & <0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & <2 \\\\ |t| & <\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we know that $t>0.$ Therefore, the eagle is descending for $t\\in (0,\\sqrt{2}).$",
